  "published": "2026-06-10",
  "insights": [
   "Levered ETFs have grown into a $300B+ AUM ecosystem controlling over $750B in equity exposure, creating a massive pool of mechanical selling pressure during market drawdowns.",
   "A 1% move in equity indices now triggers between $12B and $18B of mechanical selling from levered ETFs, significantly amplifying potential downside volatility.",
   "Levered ETF rebalancing has driven over $225B of global equity demand YTD, already surpassing the 2023 annual peak of $130B in just five months.",
   "The market's current net positive gamma position is fragile; Morgan Stanley QDS estimates the net gamma flips to short on a -4% move, leaving levered ETF selling to dominate.",
